When to use: Hovering an item in a horizontal stack (avatar row, chip group, badge cluster, segmented button) should lift the hovered item, gently lift its neighbors with a power-falloff, then snap everything back with an overshoot spring on `mouseleave`. Direction-aware easing (clean ease-in on hover, bouncy ease-out on return) is what gives the group its springy, physical feel.

